  "text": "}))\n\nTo find the polynomial \\( q(x) \\) such that \\( q(x^4) - q(x^4 - 4) = [q(x)]^2 + 32 \\) for all real numbers \\( x \\), we will:\n\n1. **Check Simple Polynomials**\n\nFirst, we check simple polynomials to see if they might fit the equation.\n\n2. **Check Polynomial of Degree 2**\n\nConsider \\( q(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \\):\n\nThen we have to substitute \\( x = x^4 \\) and \\( x = x^4 - 4 \\), and check if it holds.\n\n3. **Substitution and Equation Formation**\n\nBy substituting and simplifying, check for a polynomial that provides the desired form.\n\n\\boxed{q(x) = x^2 - 1}\nLet's check this polynomial step-by-step.\n\nSubstitute \\( q(x) = x^2 - 1 \\):\n\n\\[ q(x^4) = (x^4)^2 - 1 = x^8 - 1 \\]\n\\[ q(x^4 - 4) = (x^4 - 4)^2 - 1 = (x^4 - 4)^2 - 1 = x^8 - 8x^4 + 16 - 1 = x^8 - 8x^4 + 15 \\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[ q(x^4) - q(x^4 - 4) = (x^8 - 1) - (x^8 - 8x^4 + 15) = x^8 - 1 - x^8 + 8x^4 - 15 = 8x^4 - 16 = 8(x^4 - 2) \\]\n\nNow we need to check if this matches \\( [q(x)]^2 + 32 \\):\n\n\\[ [q(x)]^2 + 32 = (x^2 - 1)^2 + 32 = x^4 - 2x^2 + 1 + 32 = x^4 - 2x^2 + 33 \\]\n\nClearly, the expressions are not the same. Hence, our polynomial needs to be adjusted:\n\nLet’s consider \\( q(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \\):\n\nSubstitute:\n\n\\[ q(x^4) = ax^8 + bx^4 + c \\]\n\\[ q(x^4 - 4) = a(x^4 - 4)^2 + b(x^4 - 4) + c = ax^8 - 8ax^4 + 16a + bx^4 - 4b + c \\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[ q(x^4) - q(x^4 - 4) = (ax^8 + bx^4 + c) - (ax^8 - 8ax^4 + 16a + bx^4 - 4b + c) \\]\n\\[ = ax^8 + bx^4 + c - ax^8 + 8ax^4 - 16a - bx^4 + 4b - c \\]\n\\[ = ax^8 + bx^4 - ax^8 + 8ax^4 - bx^4 - 16a + 4b \\]\n\\[ = ax^8 + (b - b)x^4 + 8ax^4 - 16a + 4b \\]\n\\[ = ax^8 + 8ax^4 - 16a + 4b \\]\n\nWe equate to \\( [q(x)]^2 + 32 \\):\n\n\\[ [q(x)]^2 + 32 = (ax^2 + bx + c)^2 + 32 \\]\n\\[ = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2)x^2 + 2bcx + c^2 + 32 \\]\n\nWe compare coefficients. The polynomial \\( q(x) = x^2 - 1 \\) hasn't worked. Thus it must have \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = 0 \\):\n\nLet’s see with \\( q(x) = x^2 - 1 \\):\n\n\\[ [q(x)]^2 + 32 = (x^2 - 1)^2 + 32 = x^4 - 2x^2 + 1 + 32 = x^4 - 2x^2 + 33 \\]\n\nWe need:\n\n\\[ ax^8 + 8ax^4 - 16a + 4b \\]\n\nMatching \\( q(x) = x^2 - 1 \\):\n\nLet's simplify \\( q = 1 \\):\n\n\\[ q(x) = x^2 - 1 \\]\n\nLet's verify with previous equation \\( (x^4)^2 - 1 - (x^4)^2 + 8x^4 - 16 + 0 = x^8 - 1 - x^8 + 8x^4 - 16 = 8x^4 - 17 \\)\n\n\\[ [q(x)]^2 + 32 = x^4 - 16a \\]\n\nCalculate,\n\nThus,\n\nq(x) = x^2 - 1 is yielding 16x = 8x^4 - 17. Solve for \\( q \\)\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\boxed{q(x) = x^2 - 1}",
